cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this record format or its test suite, cite it as below."
title: "Model Intervention Records: A Conformance Test for Weight-Space Claims"
abstract: >-
  A record format and a mechanical conformance test for claims that an
  intervention changed a language model's behavior. A conforming record carries
  an executable falsifier, an invariant set with at least one metric outside the
  claim's own scoring function, and content-addressed lineage to a base
  checkpoint. The test emits eleven individual verdicts and no aggregate score,
  and so does the companion that extends the weights payload with composable
  Weight Patches. Two dependency-free implementations, in Python and Go, are
  written from the same text and agree byte for byte.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "MIR-1 contributors"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
license:
